$\begin{align}
0.8^2 &= 0.8 \cdot 0.8
\\\\
&=0.64
\end{align}$

Since $0.8$ is eight tenths, we can use fractions instead:

$\begin{align}
0.8^2 &= \dfrac{8}{10} \cdot \dfrac{8}{10}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{8 \cdot 8}{10 \cdot 10}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{64}{100}
\\\\
&=0.64 &&\gray{\text{(Sixty-four hundredths)}}
\end{align}$
